gnosis of lyme disease  um it really  begins with the discovery of berelia  backdoorfury  and it allowed for  the development of crude uh  whole borrelia burgdorferi ifas  that's immunofluorescent assays  analyzers and they just  grew the bacteria in culture and either  incubated patient serum with the whole  organism or  uh just ground up the organism and put  it on an eliza plate  that was not  terribly satisfactory because  the um  [Music]  false positive rate in  those early tests was terrible so the  predictive value  was really quite poor so  then um dressler who was working  uh with steer came  up with uh western blot criteria  and all he did was looked at what  bands were commonly showing up in people  with  with lyme disease and that was the  establishment of the so-called dressler  criteria  which was used by cdc committee  as the bands to look for in a western  blot  so to  really improve the uh specificity  of this whole process  the cdc committee said well we'll have  a crude first tier  essay that's really sensitive so we're  not going to miss  anybody that has it but we're going to  derive the specificity from the western  blot  so the western blot was put in place  because of the  poor specificity of first-year assays  and then it became codified as  the two-tier system  and that was done at the um uh  dearborn conference and that was cdc uh  really  spearheading that so  now these serologic assays  it was a lot of problems that  we now know that whole bacteria contain  many  epi epitopes that's antibody binding  sites  that are common to other bacterial  species  so we have a lot of binding  of antibody produced against other  infectious diseases the other problem  was  and i i got caught in the sensor  and that cultured bacteria can lose  plasmids  that are encoding key uh antigens  so so you keep it keep this bacteria in  culture for a while  as you pass it it becomes almost an  empty bag  and uh we didn't know that in the late  80s  and i thought